+# Evidence Contract: Pulseboard
+
+**Project**: Pulseboard
+**Project ID**: `001-pulseboard`
+**Project Archetype**: b2b_saas
+**Play Level**: build
+**Speck Version**: 10.5.0
+**Last Updated**: 2026-08-11
+
+**Scope assumption.** The current promise names browser-visible team workspaces, durable actions, and reminder delivery but no stack or recipe. Until `context.md` says otherwise, production proof means a built web client exercising a deployed API and durable store with two least-privileged workspace principals and a controlled delivery endpoint. This assumption is reversible; native, desktop, or CLI proof is not admissible for the browser claim.
+
+## 0. How this contract is read — the Four Principles
+
+- **Evaluation over verification:** evidence is collected to break a claim; a green test alone is not a readiness claim.
+- **No claim without a mechanism:** each promise below names the observed write, read, request, or terminal state that proves it.
+- **Can't reach is a finding:** an unreachable confirmation, workspace boundary, or delivery-status surface fails the applicable gate.
+- **Structural adversary:** an evaluator separate from the implementer adjudicates runtime captures and attempts the failure paths.
+
+## 1. Target Launch Platforms
+
+| Platform | Build artifact | Distribution |
+|---|---|---|
+| Web SaaS | clean production browser bundle plus deployed API, datastore, and delivery adapter | authenticated browser session at the production URL |
+
+## 2. Valid Proof Sources (per platform)
+
+### Platform: Web SaaS
+
+- A clean production build served from the deployed environment, driven through the browser UI by Playwright or an equivalent browser runner.
+- A real-session, least-privileged API read and mutation for workspace A and workspace B; the forbidden cross-workspace request must be attempted and recorded.
+- A pre-walk baseline plus a post-walk datastore read proving a new action, confirmation state, reminder, delivery attempt, or terminal failure state.
+- Delivery-provider sandbox or controlled endpoint logs tied to the reminder id, including retry and duplicate-callback evidence.
+- Browser screenshots, accessibility trees, network traces, and sanitized server logs from the same build and run; quality captures require a written per-screen judgment.
+
+### 2a. Claim-type axis
+
+| Claim type | Admissible evidence |
+|---|---|
+| correctness | test, mutation-guard, live-probe, db-catalog, ax-dump, geometry, capture, device-walk, model-eval, static |
+| visibility | live-probe, db-catalog, device-walk |
+| acceptance | live-probe, db-catalog, device-walk |
+| persistence | live-probe, db-catalog |
+| fit | ax-dump, geometry, device-walk |
+| behaviour | model-eval, device-walk |
+
+### 2b. Typed citations — the closed vocabulary and admissibility table
+
+Typed evidence uses `<citation-type>:<path>[@<sha>]`. The citation type is Speck-owned: a project may not invent one. A legacy untyped path is a P3 nudge, never evidence that the wrong substrate is admissible.
+
+| Token | Instrument |
+|---|---|
+| `test` | Unit or integration suite in the project harness. |
+| `mutation-guard` | A guard whose removal was observed to make its check red. |
+| `live-probe` | A read/write against the deployed target or real engine as a named principal. |
+| `db-catalog` | Live datastore catalog or baselined datastore read-back. |
+| `ax-dump` | Platform accessibility tree from the baked build. |
+| `geometry` | Measured container-versus-content geometry from a running screen. |
+| `capture` | Screenshot, recording, or LARP transcript. |
+| `device-walk` | Human attestation on a real device or baked artifact. |
+| `model-eval` | Control-versus-treatment on composed prompt and shipped model. |
+| `static` | Source-text, lint, type, or grep assertion. |
+
+| Claim type | Admissible citation types | Inadmissible here — and the scar that earned it |
+|---|---|---|
+| `correctness` | `test` `mutation-guard` `live-probe` `db-catalog` `static` `ax-dump` `geometry` `capture` `device-walk` `model-eval` | *(nothing — a green suite is sufficient for a correctness claim)* |
+| `visibility` | `live-probe` `db-catalog` `device-walk` | `test` · `mutation-guard` · `static` · `capture` — a mocked or bypass-capable client cannot observe real tenancy. |
+| `acceptance` | `live-probe` `db-catalog` `device-walk` | `test` · `mutation-guard` · `static` · `capture` — a mock cannot contradict what the deployed boundary accepts. |
+| `persistence` | `live-probe` `db-catalog` | `capture` · `test` · `mutation-guard` · `static` — a success screen or unbaselined read cannot prove a new durable write. |
+| `fit` | `ax-dump` `geometry` `device-walk` | `test` · `static` · `capture` · `mutation-guard` — props and jsdom geometry are not the platform tree/layout. |
+| `behaviour` | `model-eval` `device-walk` | `static` · `test` · `capture` — a prompt string's presence cannot prove model behavior. |
+
+### 2c. Promise-to-mechanism ledger
+
+| Promise | Falsifiable runtime predicate | Claim type | Required evidence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| PRM-001 | Before explicit confirmation contains non-empty action text, owner, and due date, no reminder record or delivery request exists; after confirmation, one reminder is persisted with those exact values. | persistence | baseline + live UI walk + datastore read (`live-probe:` / `db-catalog:`) |
+| PRM-002 | A real principal for workspace B cannot retrieve, search, mutate, or observe workspace A's transcript, action, or delivery status; A remains able to read its own records. | visibility | paired least-privileged live reads and forbidden mutations (`live-probe:` / `db-catalog:`) |
+| PRM-003 | For one confirmed reminder id, duplicate queueing, retry, and duplicate provider callbacks never produce more than one accepted delivery; if delivery cannot complete, the user-visible status is a truthful terminal failure rather than success or silence. | acceptance | controlled endpoint logs + persisted idempotency/terminal state + browser status (`live-probe:` / `db-catalog:` / `device-walk:`) |
+
+## 3. Invalid Proof Sources (anti-proof)
+
+- Dev-server, Storybook, component-only, mocked-auth, or fixture-only browser runs for UX-RC or higher.
+- Unit tests, source inspection, or a service-role/superuser query cited as proof of workspace isolation.
+- A post-walk datastore read without a pre-walk baseline cited as proof a reminder was created.
+- A success screenshot, queue-depth metric, or provider 2xx cited as proof of exactly-once delivery.
+- A synthetic UI state, direct API mutation, or seeded record cited as proof of the confirmation form flow.
+- Screenshots or recordings with no per-screen adversarial quality judgment.
+- Implementer-authored test harness, CI hook, or grader change used to grade the same implementation; self-declared completion is anti-proof.
+
+## 4. Required Runtime LARP / Integration Stress Tests
+
+### LARP required for UX-RC
+
+| Persona | Flow | Failure path that must be attempted | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Team facilitator | Draft an action; omit each of text, owner, and due date; then confirm all three. | Attempt schedule before every required field is explicitly confirmed. | UI recording, AX tree, network trace, baseline/post-walk store read, per-screen judgment. |
+| Workspace member A and member B | A creates transcript/action/status; B signs in in a separate session. | B reads, searches, and mutates A's known identifiers; A control read remains allowed. | Two real-session logs, response/status evidence, datastore policy evidence, screenshots. |
+| Facilitator facing delivery trouble | Confirm one reminder, inject timeout/retry/duplicate callback, then inspect status. | Duplicate enqueue and callback; permanent delivery rejection. | Correlated reminder id, endpoint logs, idempotency/terminal rows, visible status capture. |
+
+### LARP required for SHIP-RC
+
+All UX-RC flows run against the production deployment, plus a full primary-job recording for each row and a cold browser session. The evaluator records separate **DOES-IT-WORK**, **FELT-GOOD**, and **TASTE** judgments; a capture without those judgments does not pass.
+
+## 5. Quality Judgment & Scoring Protocol
+
+Green functional evidence only makes the flow eligible for judgment. For each LARP screen, the independent evaluator records a 0–10 score and a distinct note for: functional clarity, trust in confirmation, isolation/status legibility, and delivery-failure honesty. Any active P0/P1 caps the affected dimension at 4; an unjudged capture caps it at 8; a severe pixel-grounded craft defect or declared-rule violation caps TASTE below SHIP-RC.
+
+## 6. Required Static Evidence
+
+For UX-RC or higher, retain the commit SHA and deployment identifier, sanitized runtime configuration, browser screenshots and AX trees for every LARP, browser/network/server logs correlated by action or reminder id, and the baseline/post-walk datastore reads required in §2b.
+
+### 6a. CI-Enforced Gate Registry
+
+No application gate is declared yet because this workspace contains no application code or CI wiring. A later gate must declare an actual command, non-empty scope, subject count, stage, and canary before it can support a readiness claim.
+
+| Gate ID | Command / Script | Stage | Domain | Scope | Subject | Canary | Waiver |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| speck:evidence-citations | `.speck/scripts/validation/validators/validate-evidence-citations.sh specs/` | manual | evidence | `specs/**` | `citations>0` | — | — |
+| speck:probe-library | `.speck/scripts/validation/validators/validate-evidence-citations.sh --check-probe-library` | manual | evidence | `specs/projects/**` | `probe_classes>0` | — | — |
+
+## 7. Required Live-Service Evidence
+
+| Service boundary | What proves it works | What does not count |
+|---|---|---|
+| Authentication and workspace authorization | Two least-privileged deployed sessions complete allowed A reads while B's reads/searches/mutations of A's ids are denied and logged. | Mocked identity, service-role query, or a policy source review. |
+| Durable action/reminder store | Baseline, confirmation walk, and post-walk read show exact persisted values; invalid pre-confirmation attempts create no row. | Seed data or a post-walk read with no baseline. |
+| Reminder delivery adapter | A controlled endpoint/provider sandbox logs one accepted delivery for one reminder id; retry, duplicate callback, and permanent rejection expose the persisted truthful state. | A 2xx log without idempotency evidence, queue metric, or mocked adapter. |
+
+### PROFILE Gate Criteria
+
+Before SHIP-RC, the root README's product description must match the three promise IDs and must not claim delivery reliability, privacy, or launch readiness without a linked current runtime artifact.
+
+## 8. Readiness State Gate Criteria
+
+### IMPL-GREEN
+
+- CORRECT: automated tests and types cover each promise's success and named failure path.
+- ON-CONTRACT: PRM-001–003 have an implementation mapping; no runtime claim is made.
+
+### INTEGRATION-GREEN
+
+- Deployed integration proves the confirmation write, tenant boundary, and delivery-state persistence with correlated ids.
+- Every forbidden operation in §4 was genuinely attempted as the relevant least-privileged principal.
+
+### UX-RC
+
+- All UX-RC LARPs pass on a clean production build.
+- CORRECT and ON-CONTRACT have current evidence; FELT-GOOD has a naive first-time judgment; TASTE has a connoisseur judgment. These axes are not interchangeable.
+- PRM-001 proves no pre-confirmation write; PRM-002 proves both denied and allowed directions; PRM-003 proves retry/duplicate/failure truthfulness.
+
+### COMMERCIAL-RC
+
+Not applicable: the product contract makes no paid or billing promise. Billing proof is required before this state may be claimed if a commercial promise is added.
+
+### SHIP-RC
+
+- A separate evaluator reruns the §11 probe suite against the production candidate and finds no open P0/P1.
+- All evidence is fresh for the candidate SHA, all required captures are adjudicated, and the PROFILE gate passes.
+
+### SHIP
+
+- Post-deploy smoke repeats one allowed workspace action, one forbidden cross-workspace attempt, and one reminder delivery-state check against the live deployment.
+- Health/error monitoring shows no unhandled failures for the smoke run; any delivery failure is visible as its truthful terminal state.
+
+## 9. Evidence Storage
+
+| Evidence | Canonical location |
+|---|---|
+| Persona scripts | `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/personas/<persona-id>.md` |
+| Screenshots and AX trees | `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/screenshots/` and `ax-trees/` |
