+| Validation verdicts | story, epic, and project `validation-report.md` artifacts |
+
+## 10. Who Can Mark a Gate Passed
+
+The implementer may collect evidence but may not adjudicate it. A separately incentivized evaluator marks CORRECT, ON-CONTRACT, FELT-GOOD, and TASTE individually after inspecting the actual build, logs, and failure-path attempts. No gate passes from a screenshot, test count, or self-report alone.
+
+## 11. Adversarial Probe Suite
+
+| Probe | Claim challenged | Failure-path procedure | Pass condition |
+|---|---|---|
+| Confirmation bypass | PRM-001 | Submit with text, owner, or due date absent; call the mutation directly if the UI blocks. | No reminder/delivery row or request exists until all three are explicitly confirmed. |
+| Stale-confirmation race | PRM-001 | Change action fields after preview, then confirm a stale preview. | Persisted reminder exactly matches the final explicit confirmation or request is rejected. |
+| Cross-workspace direct read | PRM-002 | B requests A's transcript/action/status ids through every exposed read/search route. | Denied without record disclosure; A's same request succeeds. |
+| Cross-workspace direct mutation | PRM-002 | B attempts update/cancel/resend of A's action or reminder. | Denied; A's row and delivery state are unchanged. |
+| Client-cache second actor | PRM-002 | Sign out A, sign in B in the same browser profile, offline if cache/offline support exists. | B sees no A transcript, action, delivery status, queued request, or draft. |
+| Duplicate confirmation | PRM-003 | Double-submit and replay the same confirmation id. | One durable reminder and one accepted delivery identity exist. |
+| Retry after timeout | PRM-003 | Time out the delivery adapter after it receives the request, then retry. | Idempotency prevents duplicate accepted delivery; status stays truthful. |
+| Duplicate provider callback | PRM-003 | Replay delivery-success and delivery-failure callbacks. | State transition is idempotent and user-visible status remains consistent. |
+| Permanent provider rejection | PRM-003 | Force an unrecoverable delivery rejection. | Persisted, user-visible terminal failure names failure rather than success/pending. |
+| Status disappearance | PRM-003 | Remove or delay delivery-status response after confirmation. | UI shows a truthful degraded/unknown state, never a false delivered state. |
+| Accessibility/reachability | All | Keyboard-only and narrow-width runs reach confirmation and failure status. | Required controls and announcements are reachable and intelligible. |
+| Evidence integrity | All | Mutate the authorization/idempotency guard in a throwaway evaluation run. | The relevant negative test/probe goes red for the changed guard. |
+
+## 11a. Standard Probe Library
+
+| Probe ID | Class | Claim type | Admissible substrate | Required negative controls | Discharge artifact | Exception |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| PROBE:provenance | P1 | behaviour | render site + generator stamp + the prompt's own exemplars, judged control-vs-treatment on the composed prompt with the shipped model | rendered-with-degraded-provenance · exemplar re-read (deleting the exemplar must not leave the test green) | — | n/a:no generative surface |
+| PROBE:honest-label | P2 | persistence | the write's observed outcome read back out of the datastore against a pre-walk baseline | total-failure render · partial-failure render · the three renders differ | — | n/a:runtime not implemented yet |
+| PROBE:second-actor | P3 | visibility | A writes, teardown, B signs in on the same install, offline — once per enumerated persistence layer | signOut vs deleteAccount compared field-for-field · launch-with-data-and-no-owner-record | — | n/a:runtime not implemented yet |
+| PROBE:money-path | P4 | acceptance | the real engine as the applying principal, one run per revenue path | entitlement gate flipped and every revenue path goes red · vendor fixture cited to the vendor's field reference · per-user serialized claim write · one declared fail-posture · bounded worst case per tap | — | n/a:no revenue path |
+| PROBE:named-clock | P5 | correctness | an AST/lint rule over write handlers, cache fills and fixtures, plus the date-sensitive suites run under two timezones | a non-UTC TZ run · allowlist entries that name the audience | — | n/a:runtime not implemented yet |
+| PROBE:geometry-ax | P6 | fit | a baked build: platform AX dump plus container-vs-content geometry at 3 or more widths, numbers in the artifact | adjacent-target overlap · expected-cell presence · page overflow | — | n/a:runtime not implemented yet |
+| PROBE:substrate | P7 | correctness | §2b parity of this contract against Speck's compiled admissibility table | the parity run reports CITATION_TABLE_PARITY over a non-empty row set | — | n/a:implementation evidence not yet present |
+| PROBE:migration-dirt | P8 | acceptance | the migration applied forward on a throwaway seeded to the target's real dirty shape | pre-state REJECTED · boundary cases still refuse · one migration head after the merge | — | n/a:no schema migration surface |
+
+## 12. Stale-Proof Policy
+
+Evidence is fresh only when the build SHA matches the candidate or the changed code has been shown not to affect the claimed behavior. Evidence older than 14 days, or from a build whose relevant code changed, cannot support UX-RC or higher and must be recollected.
+
+## 13. Surrogate Proof Rule
+
+If any report cites §3 anti-proof, it must label that evidence surrogate, refuse UX-RC or higher for the affected promise, link this contract section, and schedule recollection on the admissible substrate. A test green on an empty subject, mocked identity, bypass-capable role, or stale build cache is surrogate proof.
+
+## 14. LARP Runway & Efficiency Controls
+
+Every recording captures browser build identifier, API/deployment identifier, actor/workspace ids (sanitized), reminder id, and delivery correlation id. Focused reruns may reuse a matching artifact during development, but UX-RC or higher requires a fresh clean production build.
